# Members and methods renamed in one run: 3024 edits across 68 files apply with
# 0 conflicts, //... rebuilds clean, and a second pass has nothing left to do.
# The styles are chosen so the two rules cannot land on the same name (see the
# ruleset), and cpp_format refuses the combinations that can.
#
# This is the only scenario that renames member functions, and the trail from
# 14868 errors is the method half growing up. 11044 once the dependent-token
# sidecar carried a rule index (one rule's veto had been cancelling another
# rule's resolution); 3771 once member function templates mapped back to their
# pattern and the spelling audit started declining every unresolved overload
# set a template leaves behind (Init(p) with dependent arguments, a
# using-declaration of a dependent base's member, gmock's MOCK_METHOD argument
# that only ever exists pasted into gmock_DoThis); 10 once a derived class
# declaring the new name was checked per use; green once a declaration spelled
# as an argument of a macro that also pastes with ## was declined outright --
# ACTION_P3(Plus, foo, bar, baz) makes a member foo and a typedef foo_type that
# renaming foo would have turned into foo__type.
#
# Every one of those was found here rather than by inspection. The method
# names that stay put are declined and reported -- the protocol names the
# language calls implicitly, and everything the audit could not account for.
#
# NB: this file is sourced by bash, so values must not contain backticks or the
# dollar sign.
REPO=googletest
RULESET=member_trailing_method_snake
EXPECT=pass
